  Algebra with AI-Supported Instruction</h2></span><p class="text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm">December 4, 2024</p></div><div class="bg-primary/10 dark:bg-primary/20 text-primary rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium whitespace-nowrap mt-[1px] ml-2">91<!-- -->% Match</div></div><div class="grid gap-2"><div class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 overflow-hidden mb-1"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-user w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0"><path d="M19 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H9a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"></circle></svg><span class="line-clamp-1">Otero Nancy, Druga Stefania, Lan Andrew</span></div><div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 overflow-hidden -ml-1 _ttp"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-tags ml-1 w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0 scale-125"><path d="m15 5 6.3 6.3a2.4 2.4 0 0 1 0 3.4L17 19"></path><path d="M9.586 5.586A2 2 0 0 0 8.172 5H3a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v5.172a2 2 0 0 0 .586 1.414L8.29 18.29a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 3.42 0l3.58-3.58a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 0-3.42z"></path><circle cx="6.5" cy="9.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg><div class="flex items-center gap-2 overflow-scroll scroll no-scrollbar"><div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:ring-offset-2 border-transparent bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap" title="cs.HC" style="background-color:#3cb44b;color:#000">Human-Computer Interaction</div><div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:ring-offset-2 border-transparent bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap" title="cs.CY" style="background-color:#3cb44b;color:#000">Computers and Society</div></div></div></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-6 items-end"><div class="relative"><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1 line-clamp-4">This study introduces an evaluation benchmark for middle school algebra to be
used in artificial intelligence(AI) based educational platforms. The goal is to
support the design of AI systems that can enhance learner conceptual
understanding of algebra by taking into account their current level of algebra
comprehension. The data set comprises 55 misconceptions about algebra, common
errors, and 220 diagnostic examples identified in previous peer-reviewed
studies. We provide an ...</p><span class="inline-block absolute -bottom-0.5 -right-4 p-1 pl-6 cursor-pointer bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-background max-lg:hidden"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-4 h-4 m-auto transition-transform"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></div><div class="flex gap-2 md:flex-col-reverse md:justify-end"><span class="cursor-pointer inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium ring-offset-background transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90 h-10 px-4 py-2 shrink-0 group"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles w-4 h-4 mr-2"><path d="M9.937 15.5A2 2 0 0 0 8.5 14.063l-6.135-1.582a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.962L8.5 9.936A2 2 0 0 0 9.937 8.5l1.582-6.135a.5.5 0 0 1 .963 0L14.063 8.5A2 2 0 0 0 15.5 9.937l6.135 1.581a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .964L15.5 14.063a2 2 0 0 0-1.437 1.437l-1.582 6.135a.5.5 0 0 1-.963 0z"></path><path d="M20 3v4"></path><path d="M22 5h-4"></path><path d="M4 17v2"></path><path d="M5 18H3"></path></svg>Find Similar</span><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.03765" target="_blank" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium ring-offset-background focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 text-secondary-foreground h-10 px-4 py-2 shrink-0 bg-primary/10 dark:bg-primary/20 hover:bg-[#b31b1b] dark:hover:bg-[#b31b1b] hover:text-white transition-colors">View on arXiv</a></div></div></div><div class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 grid gap-4 my-10 overflow-hidden rounded-lg p-6 transition-opacity border shadow-md"><div class="flex justify-between items-start"><div class="grid gap-1"><span class="cursor-pointer"><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold line-clamp-2">Error Classification of Large Language Models on Math Word Problems: A
  Dynamically Adaptive Framework</h2></span><p class="text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm">January 26, 2025</p></div><div class="bg-primary/10 dark:bg-primary/20 text-primary rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium whitespace-nowrap mt-[1px] ml-2">91<!-- -->% Match</div></div><div class="grid gap-2"><div class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 overflow-hidden mb-1"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-user w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0"><path d="M19 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H9a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"></circle></svg><span class="flex overflow-hidden"><span class="whitespace-nowrap overflow-ellipsis overflow-hidden">Yuhong Sun, Zhangyue Yin, Xuanjing Huang</span><span class="whitespace-nowrap">, ... , <!-- -->Zhao Hui</span></span></div><div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 overflow-hidden -ml-1 _ttp"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-tags ml-1 w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0 scale-125"><path d="m15 5 6.3 6.3a2.4 2.4 0 0 1 0 3.4L17 19"></path><path d="M9.586 5.586A2 2 0 0 0 8.172 5H3a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v5.172a2 2 0 0 0 .586 1.414L8.29 18.29a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 3.42 0l3.58-3.58a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 0-3.42z"></path><circle cx="6.5" cy="9.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg><div class="flex items-center gap-2 overflow-scroll scroll no-scrollbar"><div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:ring-offset-2 border-transparent bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap" title="cs.CL" style="background-color:#3cb44b;color:#000">Computation and Language</div></div></div></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-6 items-end"><div class="relative"><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1 line-clamp-4">Large Language Models (LLMs) have demonstrated remarkable capabilities across
various domains. Math Word Problems (MWPs) serve as a crucial benchmark for
evaluating LLMs&#x27; reasoning abilities. While most research primarily focuses on
improving accuracy, it often neglects understanding and addressing the
underlying patterns of errors. Current error classification methods rely on
static and predefined categories, which limit their ability to capture the full
spectrum of error pa...</p><span class="inline-block absolute -bottom-0.5 -right-4 p-1 pl-6 cursor-pointer bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-background max-lg:hidden"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-4 h-4 m-auto transition-transform"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></div><div class="flex gap-2 md:flex-col-reverse md:justify-end"><span class="cursor-pointer inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium ring-offset-background transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90 h-10 px-4 py-2 shrink-0 group"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles w-4 h-4 mr-2"><path d="M9.937 15.5A2 2 0 0 0 8.5 14.063l-6.135-1.582a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.962L8.5 9.936A2 2 0 0 0 9.937 8.5l1.582-6.135a.5.5 0 0 1 .963 0L14.063 8.5A2 2 0 0 0 15.5 9.937l6.135 1.581a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .964L15.5 14.063a2 2 0 0 0-1.437 1.437l-1.582 6.135a.5.5 0 0 1-.963 0z"></path><path d="M20 3v4"></path><path d="M22 5h-4"></path><path d="M4 17v2"></path><path d="M5 18H3"></path></svg>Find Similar</span><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.15581" target="_blank" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium ring-offset-background focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 text-secondary-foreground h-10 px-4 py-2 shrink-0 bg-primary/10 dark:bg-primary/20 hover:bg-[#b31b1b] dark:hover:bg-[#b31b1b] hover:text-white transition-colors">View on arXiv</a></div></div></div><div class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 grid gap-4 my-10 overflow-hidden rounded-lg p-6 transition-opacity border shadow-md"><div class="flex justify-between items-start"><div class="grid gap-1"><span class="cursor-pointer"><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold line-clamp-2">AI-Driven Virtual Teacher for Enhanced Educational Efficiency:
  Leveraging Large Pretrain Models for Autonomous Error Analysis and Correction</h2></span><p class="text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm">September 14, 2024</p></div><div class="bg-primary/10 dark:bg-primary/20 text-primary rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium whitespace-nowrap mt-[1px] ml-2">91<!-- -->% Match</div></div><div class="grid gap-2"><div class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 overflow-hidden mb-1"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-user w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0"><path d="M19 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H9a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"></circle></svg><span class="flex overflow-hidden"><span class="whitespace-nowrap overflow-ellipsis overflow-hidden">Tianlong Xu, Yi-Fan Zhang, Zhendong Chu</span><span class="whitespace-nowrap">, ... , <!-- -->Wen Qingsong</span></span></div><div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 overflow-hidden -ml-1 _ttp"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-tags ml-1 w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0 scale-125"><path d="m15 5 6.3 6.3a2.4 2.4 0 0 1 0 3.4L17 19"></path><path d="M9.586 5.586A2 2 0 0 0 8.172 5H3a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v5.172a2 2 0 0 0 .586 1.414L8.29 18.29a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 3.42 0l3.58-3.58a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 0-3.42z"></path><circle cx="6.5" cy="9.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg><div class="flex items-center gap-2 overflow-scroll scroll no-scrollbar"><span><div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:ring-offset-2 border-transparent bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap" title="cs.CV" style="background-color:#3cb44b;color:#000">Computer Vision and Pattern ...</div></span><div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:ring-offset-2 border-transparent bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap" title="cs.AI" style="background-color:#3cb44b;color:#000">Artificial Intelligence</div><div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:ring-offset-2 border-transparent bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap" title="cs.MM" style="background-color:#3cb44b;color:#000">Multimedia</div></div></div></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-6 items-end"><div class="relative"><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1 line-clamp-4">Students frequently make mistakes while solving mathematical problems, and
traditional error correction methods are both time-consuming and
labor-intensive. This paper introduces an innovative \textbf{V}irtual
\textbf{A}I \textbf{T}eacher system designed to autonomously analyze and
correct student \textbf{E}rrors (VATE). Leveraging advanced large language
models (LLMs), the system uses student drafts as a primary source for error
