flex items-center gap-2 overflow-scroll scroll no-scrollbar"><div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:ring-offset-2 border-transparent bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap" title="cs.CL" style="background-color:#3cb44b;color:#000">Computation and Language</div><div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:ring-offset-2 border-transparent bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap" title="cs.AI" style="background-color:#3cb44b;color:#000">Artificial Intelligence</div></div></div></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-6 items-end"><div class="relative"><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1 line-clamp-4">Scaling high-quality tutoring is a major challenge in education. Because of
the growing demand, many platforms employ novice tutors who, unlike
professional educators, struggle to effectively address student mistakes and
thus fail to seize prime learning opportunities for students. In this paper, we
explore the potential for large language models (LLMs) to assist math tutors in
remediating student mistakes. We present ReMath, a benchmark co-developed with
experienced math tea...</p><span class="inline-block absolute -bottom-0.5 -right-4 p-1 pl-6 cursor-pointer bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-background max-lg:hidden"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-4 h-4 m-auto transition-transform"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></div><div class="flex gap-2 md:flex-col-reverse md:justify-end"><span class="cursor-pointer inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium ring-offset-background transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90 h-10 px-4 py-2 shrink-0 group"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles w-4 h-4 mr-2"><path d="M9.937 15.5A2 2 0 0 0 8.5 14.063l-6.135-1.582a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.962L8.5 9.936A2 2 0 0 0 9.937 8.5l1.582-6.135a.5.5 0 0 1 .963 0L14.063 8.5A2 2 0 0 0 15.5 9.937l6.135 1.581a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .964L15.5 14.063a2 2 0 0 0-1.437 1.437l-1.582 6.135a.5.5 0 0 1-.963 0z"></path><path d="M20 3v4"></path><path d="M22 5h-4"></path><path d="M4 17v2"></path><path d="M5 18H3"></path></svg>Find Similar</span><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.10648" target="_blank" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium ring-offset-background focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 text-secondary-foreground h-10 px-4 py-2 shrink-0 bg-primary/10 dark:bg-primary/20 hover:bg-[#b31b1b] dark:hover:bg-[#b31b1b] hover:text-white transition-colors">View on arXiv</a></div></div></div><div class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 grid gap-4 my-10 overflow-hidden rounded-lg p-6 transition-opacity border shadow-md"><div class="flex justify-between items-start"><div class="grid gap-1"><span class="cursor-pointer"><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold line-clamp-2">Data-Driven Methods for Solving Algebra Word Problems</h2></span><p class="text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm">April 28, 2018</p></div><div class="bg-primary/10 dark:bg-primary/20 text-primary rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium whitespace-nowrap mt-[1px] ml-2">90<!-- -->% Match</div></div><div class="grid gap-2"><div class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 overflow-hidden mb-1"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-user w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0"><path d="M19 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H9a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"></circle></svg><span class="line-clamp-1">Benjamin Robaidek, Rik Koncel-Kedziorski, Hannaneh Hajishirzi</span></div><div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 overflow-hidden -ml-1 _ttp"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-tags ml-1 w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0 scale-125"><path d="m15 5 6.3 6.3a2.4 2.4 0 0 1 0 3.4L17 19"></path><path d="M9.586 5.586A2 2 0 0 0 8.172 5H3a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v5.172a2 2 0 0 0 .586 1.414L8.29 18.29a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 3.42 0l3.58-3.58a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 0-3.42z"></path><circle cx="6.5" cy="9.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg><div class="flex items-center gap-2 overflow-scroll scroll no-scrollbar"><div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:ring-offset-2 border-transparent bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap" title="cs.AI" style="background-color:#3cb44b;color:#000">Artificial Intelligence</div><div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:ring-offset-2 border-transparent bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap" title="cs.CL" style="background-color:#3cb44b;color:#000">Computation and Language</div></div></div></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-6 items-end"><div class="relative"><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1 line-clamp-4">We explore contemporary, data-driven techniques for solving math word
problems over recent large-scale datasets. We show that well-tuned neural
equation classifiers can outperform more sophisticated models such as sequence
to sequence and self-attention across these datasets. Our error analysis
indicates that, while fully data driven models show some promise, semantic and
world knowledge is necessary for further advances.</p></div><div class="flex gap-2 md:flex-col-reverse md:justify-end"><span class="cursor-pointer inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium ring-offset-background transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90 h-10 px-4 py-2 shrink-0 group"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles w-4 h-4 mr-2"><path d="M9.937 15.5A2 2 0 0 0 8.5 14.063l-6.135-1.582a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.962L8.5 9.936A2 2 0 0 0 9.937 8.5l1.582-6.135a.5.5 0 0 1 .963 0L14.063 8.5A2 2 0 0 0 15.5 9.937l6.135 1.581a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .964L15.5 14.063a2 2 0 0 0-1.437 1.437l-1.582 6.135a.5.5 0 0 1-.963 0z"></path><path d="M20 3v4"></path><path d="M22 5h-4"></path><path d="M4 17v2"></path><path d="M5 18H3"></path></svg>Find Similar</span><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.10718" target="_blank" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium ring-offset-background focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 text-secondary-foreground h-10 px-4 py-2 shrink-0 bg-primary/10 dark:bg-primary/20 hover:bg-[#b31b1b] dark:hover:bg-[#b31b1b] hover:text-white transition-colors">View on arXiv</a></div></div></div><div class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 grid gap-4 my-10 overflow-hidden rounded-lg p-6 transition-opacity border shadow-md"><div class="flex justify-between items-start"><div class="grid gap-1"><span class="cursor-pointer"><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold line-clamp-2">MathMistake Checker: A Comprehensive Demonstration for Step-by-Step Math
  Problem Mistake Finding by Prompt-Guided LLMs</h2></span><p class="text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm">March 6, 2025</p></div><div class="bg-primary/10 dark:bg-primary/20 text-primary rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium whitespace-nowrap mt-[1px] ml-2">90<!-- -->% Match</div></div><div class="grid gap-2"><div class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 overflow-hidden mb-1"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-user w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0"><path d="M19 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H9a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"></circle></svg><span class="flex overflow-hidden"><span class="whitespace-nowrap overflow-ellipsis overflow-hidden">Tianyang Zhang, Zhuoxuan Jiang, Haotian Zhang</span><span class="whitespace-nowrap">, ... , <!-- -->Zhang Shaohua</span></span></div><div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 overflow-hidden -ml-1 _ttp"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-tags ml-1 w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0 scale-125"><path d="m15 5 6.3 6.3a2.4 2.4 0 0 1 0 3.4L17 19"></path><path d="M9.586 5.586A2 2 0 0 0 8.172 5H3a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v5.172a2 2 0 0 0 .586 1.414L8.29 18.29a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 3.42 0l3.58-3.58a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 0-3.42z"></path><circle cx="6.5" cy="9.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg><div class="flex items-center gap-2 overflow-scroll scroll no-scrollbar"><div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:ring-offset-2 border-transparent bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap" title="cs.AI" style="background-color:#3cb44b;color:#000">Artificial Intelligence</div></div></div></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-6 items-end"><div class="relative"><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1 line-clamp-4">We propose a novel system, MathMistake Checker, designed to automate
step-by-step mistake finding in mathematical problems with lengthy answers
through a two-stage process. The system aims to simplify grading, increase
efficiency, and enhance learning experiences from a pedagogical perspective. It
integrates advanced technologies, including computer vision and the
chain-of-thought capabilities of the latest large language models (LLMs). Our
system supports open-ended grading ...</p><span class="inline-block absolute -bottom-0.5 -right-4 p-1 pl-6 cursor-pointer bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-background max-lg:hidden"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-4 h-4 m-auto transition-transform"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></div><div class="flex gap-2 md:flex-col-reverse md:justify-end"><span class="cursor-pointer inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium ring-offset-background transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90 h-10 px-4 py-2 shrink-0 group"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles w-4 h-4 mr-2"><path d="M9.937 15.5A2 2 0 0 0 8.5 14.063l-6.135-1.582a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.962L8.5 9.936A2 2 0 0 0 9.937 8.5l1.582-6.135a.5.5 0 0 1 .963 0L14.063 8.5A2 2 0 0 0 15.5 9.937l6.135 1.581a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .964L15.5 14.063a2 2 0 0 0-1.437 1.437l-1.582 6.135a.5.5 0 0 1-.963 0z"></path><path d="M20 3v4"></path><path d="M22 5h-4"></path><path d="M4 17v2"></path><path d="M5 18H3"></path></svg>Find Similar</span><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.04291" target="_blank" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium ring-offset-background focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 text-secondary-foreground h-10 px-4 py-2 shrink-0 bg-primary/10 dark:bg-primary/20 hover:bg-[#b31b1b] dark:hover:bg-[#b31b1b] hover:text-white transition-colors">View on arXiv</a></div></div></div><div class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-950 grid gap-4 my-10 overflow-hidden rounded-lg p-6 transition-opacity border shadow-md"><div class="flex justify-between items-start"><div class="grid gap-1"><span class="cursor-pointer"><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold line-clamp-2">Solving Math Word Problems by Combining Language Models With Symbolic
  Solvers</h2></span><p class="text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm">April 16, 2023</p></div><div class="bg-primary/10 dark:bg-primary/20 text-primary rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium whitespace-nowrap mt-[1px] ml-2">90<!-- -->% Match</div></div><div class="grid gap-2"><div class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 overflow-hidden mb-1"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-user w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0"><path d="M19 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H9a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"></circle></svg><span class="flex overflow-hidden"><span class="whitespace-nowrap overflow-ellipsis overflow-hidden">Joy He-Yueya, Gabriel Poesia</span><span class="whitespace-nowrap">, ... , <!-- -->Goodman Noah D.</span></span></div><div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 overflow-hidden -ml-1 _ttp"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-tags ml-1 w-4 h-4 flex-shrink-0 scale-125"><path d="m15 5 6.3 6.3a2.4 2.4 0 0 1 0 3.4L17 19"></path><path d="M9.586 5.586A2 2 0 0 0 8.172 5H3a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v5.172a2 2 0 0 0 .586 1.414L8.29 18.29a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 3.42 0l3.58-3.58a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 0-3.42z"></path><circle cx="6.5" cy="9.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg><div class="flex items-center gap-2 overflow-scroll scroll no-scrollbar"><div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:ring-offset-2 border-transparent bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap" title="cs.CL" style="background-color:#3cb44b;color:#000">Computation and Language</div><div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring focus:ring-offset-2 border-transparent bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 whitespace-nowrap" title="cs.AI" style="background-color:#3cb44b;color:#000">Artificial Intelligence</div></div></div></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-6 items-end"><div class="relative"><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1 line-clamp-4">Automatically generating high-quality step-by-step solutions to math word
problems has many applications in education. Recently, combining large language
models (LLMs) with external tools to perform complex reasoning and calculation
has emerged as a promising direction for solving math word problems, but prior
approaches such as Program-Aided Language model (PAL) are biased towards simple
procedural problems and less effective for problems that require declarative
reasoning. ...</p><span class="inline-block absolute -bottom-0.5 -right-4 p-1 pl-6 cursor-pointer bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent to-background max-lg:hidden"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-4 h-4 m-auto transition-transform"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></span></div><div class="flex gap-2 md:flex-col-reverse md:justify-end"><span class="cursor-pointer inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium ring-offset-background transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90 h-10 px-4 py-2 shrink-0 group"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-sparkles w-4 h-4 mr-2"><path d="M9.937 15.5A2 2 0 0 0 8.5 14.063l-6.135-1.582a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.962L8.5 9.936A2 2 0 0 0 9.937 8.5l1.582-6.135a.5.5 0 0 1 .963 0L14.063 8.5A2 2 0 0 0 15.5 9.937l6.135 1.581a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .964L15.5 14.063a2 2 0 0 0-1.437 1.437l-1.582 6.135a.5.5 0 0 1-.963 0z"></path><path d="M20 3v4"></path><path d="M22 5h-4"></path><path d="M4 17v2"></path><path d="M5 18H3"></path></svg>Find Similar</span><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.09102" target="_blank" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium ring-offset-background focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 text-secondary-foreground h-10 px-4 py-2 shrink-0 bg-primary/10 dark:bg-primary/20 hover:bg-[#b31b1b] dark:hover:bg-[#b31b1b] hover:text-wh